{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPLYHF4J8sYqZpdnNKWL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found a positive but small effect. A 1-SD increase in supplier diversity goes with 0.69 points higher 2023 export growth (robust SE 0.24, p = 0.004, 95% CI 0.22 to 1.16). Export growth averages about 100, so this is modest. The data are a single cross-section, so the estimate is causal only if the controls remove all confounding. I can't rule out unobserved confounders.\n\n**Preferred specification:** OLS of 2023 export growth on supplier diversity, with all the 2020 pre-period firm characteristics as controls (N = 2000).\n\n**Controls changed the answer a lot.** Without controls the estimate is 2.55, about 3.7 times larger. Larger, more experienced firms have both more suppliers and higher growth, so the raw figure is confounded.\n\n**One variable I left out on purpose:** `buyer_rating_2023`. It is measured after the supplier data, so it may be partly a result of diversification. Adding it flips the estimate to −2.12, which I read as an artefact of controlling for something downstream, not a real negative effect.\n\n**Specifications:** I estimated five in total. The other two are a version with only size, experience and 2020 growth as controls (0.69), and one that adds a squared term for diversity (0.69 on the linear term). The squared term gave no reason to prefer a nonlinear model.\n\nI picked the preferred specification on causal-ordering grounds, not by which result looked best for your hypothesis. The report lists every specification, including the two I didn't prefer.\n\nFiles are in `<run_root>/runs/pilot_261025/A2_P1_p03_r1/gen/`:\n- `report.md`\n- `final_answer.json`\n- `a.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1657,"cache_read_input_tokens":10850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1657,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":581,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c77a36a3-cce6-46d5-b46f-a0c59387b81b","uuid":"1d123bb6-5a08-4e79-8ff9-aaa15bbab097"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":32741,"duration_api_ms":35413,"num_turns":9,"result":"I found a positive but small effect. A 1-SD increase in supplier diversity goes with 0.69 points higher 2023 export growth (robust SE 0.24, p = 0.004, 95% CI 0.22 to 1.16). Export growth averages about 100, so this is modest. The data are a single cross-section, so the estimate is causal only if the controls remove all confounding. I can't rule out unobserved confounders.\n\n**Preferred specification:** OLS of 2023 export growth on supplier diversity, with all the 2020 pre-period firm characteristics as controls (N = 2000).\n\n**Controls changed the answer a lot.** Without controls the estimate is 2.55, about 3.7 times larger. Larger, more experienced firms have both more suppliers and higher growth, so the raw figure is confounded.\n\n**One variable I left out on purpose:** `buyer_rating_2023`. It is measured after the supplier data, so it may be partly a result of diversification. Adding it flips the estimate to −2.12, which I read as an artefact of controlling for something downstream, not a real negative effect.\n\n**Specifications:** I estimated five in total. The other two are a version with only size, experience and 2020 growth as controls (0.69), and one that adds a squared term for diversity (0.69 on the linear term). The squared term gave no reason to prefer a nonlinear model.\n\nI picked the preferred specification on causal-ordering grounds, not by which result looked best for your hypothesis. The report lists every specification, including the two I didn't prefer.\n\nFiles are in `<run_root>/runs/pilot_261025/A2_P1_p03_r1/gen/`:\n- `report.md`\n- `final_answer.json`\n- `a.py`","session_id":"c77a36a3-cce6-46d5-b46f-a0c59387b81b","total_cost_usd":0.09009675,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6153,"cache_read_input_tokens":48300,"output_tokens":2893,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0}